  "question": {
    "text": "An <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> metal block of dimensions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is lying on a table with its face of largest area touching the table. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then the minimum amount of work done in making it stand with its length vertical is",
